-- title:
--   Chart overlap agreement for invariant functions on the unramified layer
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. The arithmetic data consist of: a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`h\pi`) such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$; a characteristic-zero domain $O^{nr}$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to the group of hypotheses `hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`, `hOnr_alg`, `hOnr_closed`, `hFr`: $O^{nr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{nr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo it, every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for every $x$; finally a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   The group-theoretic data consist of a group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G\to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma$, with `hcent` asserting that some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z)=2$, and `hodd` that some $w\in\Gamma$ has $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w)=1$; a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `h\Gamma'` as the set of $x\in\Gamma$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ even; a homomorphism $\rho : G\to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`h\rho`), such that the action of $\rho(\Gamma')$ on the vertices [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) of the tree of homothety classes of full lattices has finite vertex stabilisers (`hdisc`) and finitely many orbits, in the form of a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit (`hcocpt`); the matrix $g_1$ with $(g_1)=\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`); and a subgroup $N\le \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ with $N\le\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`), $N$ normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`) and of nonzero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`), together with a term `DM : MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, the structure packaging a tower of schemes `DM.Z n` proper and flat over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transition maps, an affine-neighbourhood property, and a moduli map `DM.q` assigning to a Deligne datum over a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal{O}$-algebra a point of `DM.Z n`, natural, compatible with the transitions and invariant under $N$.
--
--   On top of this there is a second tower: schemes $X n$ with structure maps $xb_n : X n\to\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n : X n\to X(n+1)$, a finite group $G_2$ acting through $a_n : G_2\to\mathrm{Aut}(X n)$, projections $pr_{1,n} : X n\to DM.Z\,n$ and $pr_{2,n} : X n\to \mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$, where $\mathcal{O}_2 =$ `AlgHom.equalizer` of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, i.e. the subalgebra of $O^{nr}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^2$; a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma\to G_2$; and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$. These are subject to the following group of hypotheses: `hcart` (each square formed by $xt_n$, $xb_n$, $xb_{n+1}$ and the quotient map $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ is a pullback), `hproper` and `hflat` (each $xb_n$ is proper and flat), `haff` (every finite subset of $X n$ lies in an affine open), `ha_over` and `ha_xt` (the $G_2$-action is over the base and commutes with the transitions), `hX` (each $X n$ is the fibre product of $pr_{1,n}$ along $DM.zb_n$ and of $pr_{2,n}$ along the map induced by $\mathcal{O}\to\mathcal{O}_2$), `hxb`, `hxt₁`, `hxt₂` (the structure map and the transitions are compatible with the two projections), `h\thetasurj` and `h\thetaker` ($\theta$ is surjective and $\theta\gamma=1$ exactly when $\rho\gamma\in N$), `hFr₂` ($\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$), `ha_pr₂` (for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ followed by $pr_{2,n}$ equals $pr_{2,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$), and `ha_pr₁` (if $P'$ is the pullback of the Deligne datum $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, in the sense that the line of $P'$ at each full lattice $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P$ at $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}M$, and $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B\to X n$ has $x$ followed by $pr_{1,n}$ equal to `DM.q n B hB P`, then $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $pr_{1,n}$ equals `DM.q n B hB P'`).
--
--   Further data: a quotient tower `DQ : TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`, consisting of schemes `DQ.Y n` proper and flat over $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ with cartesian transitions and finite surjective $G_2$-invariant projections `DQ.p n : X n ⟶ DQ.Y n` together with a local universal property; and a moduli map $q$ which to each $n$, each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ (`hB`) and each point of the product functor `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)`, that is, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $O^{nr}\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, assigns a morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to DQ.Y\,n$. The hypotheses on $q$ are: `hqdef` (if $\psi : O^{nr}\to B$ factors through $\psi_2$ on $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$ as in `h\psi₂`, $P$ is a Deligne datum and $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B\to X n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $pr_{1,n}$ equal to `DM.q n B hB P` and $x$ followed by $pr_{2,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi_2)$, then $q\,n\,B\,hB\,(\psi,P)$ is $x$ followed by `DQ.p n`), `hqover` (the points of $q$ lie over $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the structure map of $B$), `hqnat` (naturality in $B$), `hqyt` (compatibility with the transitions `DQ.yt n`), and `hqinv` (for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, $q$ takes the same value on $x$ and on $x'$ whenever `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'`, i.e. the first component of $x'$ is the first component of $x$ precomposed with $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and the second component of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$).
--
--   The unramified layer is given by `Pr : MumfordTower.NrPresentation 𝒪 π K₀ g₁ N DM Onr Fr X xb xt G₂ a pr₁ pr₂ ((Γ'.subgroupOf Γ).map θ)`, packaging schemes `Pr.X' n` over $O^{nr}/\pi^{n+1}$ obtained from $X n$ by the base change `Pr.qX n`, with transitions `Pr.xt'`, a $G_2$-action `Pr.a'` and chart morphisms `Pr.κ' h n` from $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $A_n :=$ `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ into `Pr.X' n`; here `chartERing R π r` is the localisation of $R[\xi,\eta]/(\xi\eta-\pi)$ at the relevant discriminant element, with distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`. Over this there is a quotient tower `D' : TowerQuotientDatum Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) Pr.X' Pr.xb' Pr.xt' G₂ Pr.a'`, and comparison morphisms $rY_n : D'.Y\,n\to DQ.Y\,n$ with `hrY` (each square formed by $rY_n$, `D'.yb n`, `DQ.yb n` and the map induced by $\mathcal{O}\to O^{nr}$ on the quotients by $\pi^{n+1}$ is a pullback), `hrY_p` (`D'.p n` followed by $rY_n$ equals `Pr.qX n` followed by `DQ.p n`) and `hrY_yt` (compatibility with the transitions).
--
--   Chart-theoretic data: for every $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n$ an open subscheme $U(h,n)$ of $D'.Y\,n$ whose underlying set is the image of the base map of `Pr.κ' h n` followed by `D'.p n` (`hU`), and a ring homomorphism $c(h,n)$ from the sections of $D'.Y\,n$ over $U(h,n)$ to $A_n$, together with `hκU` (the preimage of $U(h,n)$ under that chart composite is the whole of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_n$) and `hc` ($c(h,n)$ is the pullback of sections along the chart composite, read through the canonical isomorphism between global sections of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_n$ and $A_n$).
--
--   Now fix $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a family $\mathrm{fam}(m)\in A_m$ for all $m$, compatible with the transition maps $A_{m+1}\to A_m$ in the sense that the induced map sends $\mathrm{fam}(m+1)$ to $\mathrm{fam}(m)$ (`hfam`). The invariance hypothesis `hinv` requires: for every $m$, every commutative ring $B$ that is simultaneously an $\mathcal{O}$- and an $O^{nr}$-algebra compatibly, with the image of $\pi$ in $B$ nilpotent, every pair of $O^{nr}$-algebra maps $\bar{x},\bar{x}' : A_m\to B$ and all Deligne data $d,d',P,P'$ over $B$ for $\pi$ and $K_0$: if $d$ lies in the edge chart determined by the standard full lattice and its $g_1$-translate, with coordinates given by $\bar{x}$ — that is, the line of $d$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar{x}(\xi)\otimes e_0 + 1\otimes e_1$, the line of $d$ at $g_1\cdot$(standard lattice) is the image under the base-changed action of $g_1$ of the span of $1\otimes e_0 + \bar{x}(\eta)\otimes e_1$, and $d$ satisfies `DeligneDatum.InEdgeChart`, i.e. the edge nondegeneracy conditions at every prime ideal of $B$ for the pair (standard lattice, its $g_1$-translate) — and if $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $\bar{x}'$ in place of $\bar{x}$, and if $d$ is the pullback of $P$ along $h^{-1}$ and $d'$ the pullback of $P'$ along $h^{-1}$, and if there exists $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ such that $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, then $\bar{x}(\mathrm{fam}(m)) = \bar{x}'(\mathrm{fam}(m))$.
--
--   Under all of the above, let $m$ be a natural number, $g\in G_2$, $B$ a commutative ring (with no algebra structure imposed) and $x,x' : A_m\to B$ ring homomorphisms such that $\mathrm{Spec}(x)$ followed by `Pr.κ' h m` equals $\mathrm{Spec}(x')$ followed by `Pr.κ' h m` and then by the automorphism `(Pr.a' m g).hom` (`hpt`). The conclusion is the single equality
--   $$x(\mathrm{fam}(m)) = x'(\mathrm{fam}(m))$$
--   in $B$.
--
--   This is the overlap-agreement step in the construction of invariant functions on the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld formal quotient: it says that a compatible, $\Gamma'$-invariant family of chart functions takes the same value at two points of a chart that differ by an automorphism of the tower, which is what makes the function well defined on the quotient. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_sections_of_inv), and rests on the Zariski-local relation statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_related_locally`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_related_locally) together with the base-change description of the chart ring and the existence and uniqueness of Deligne data in an edge chart.
